--- !u!114 &1646601673
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1646601671}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3ff6acaa8b9f1994499dd387e6188532, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  Comments: 'This scene demonstrates the use of a MIDI file to drive animation behaviors
    as well as optionally using the 3rd free plugin MIDI Jack to receive signals
    from MIDI devices. MIDI files may contain one or multiple tracks and can be exported
    from most DAWs.


    When properly configured, this scene demonstrates how to
    receive input from a MIDI device connected to the computer. Enter play mode to
    test. By default it is mapped to index 60 which corresponds to middle C on a
    standard keyboard. Settings are stored in PlayerPrefs for subsequent runs.


    To
    map a different MIDI input, click the programming button in the upper right corner
    to enter listening mode. The first key pressed is recorded and mapped to the
    input, showing the new code assigned. This setup may be replicated for as many
    MIDI inputs as you wish. Mapping configurations may be saved in the scene for
    future use.'
  Warning: 'MIDI files must be renamed with the file extension ".bytes" for the asset
    to be imported correctly in Unity. Any other file extension will result in an
    unreadable file.



    MIDI Jack Installation

    Please note that MIDI Jack
    is not included with Timeflow but may be downloaded and installed for free from
    GitHub. See the link below. Once installed, please be sure to complete the setup
    by adding MIDIJACK to the Scripting Define Symbols in player settings. Please
    refer to the documenation for complete setup instructions. '
  URLTitle: MIDI Documentation
  URL: https://axongenesis.gitbook.io/timeflow/reference/behaviors/midi
  URL2Title: Download MIDI Jack
  URL2: https://github.com/keijiro/MidiJack
